// A `for` loop carrying a value (owner ruling 2026-09-29): `break s` exits with `s`, and a
// loop that can run out also yields `null`, so the value is `string | null`. The proof prints
// the element the break chose, which neither the null nor the first element would.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@PRELUDE@@
function words(): string[] { ["a", "bb", "ccc"] }
// @@VALUE@@
for s in words() { if s.length > 1 { break s } }
// @@TYPE@@
string | null
// @@PROOF@@
print(v ?? "none")
// @@WANT@@
bb
// @@TEST@@
v != null
// @@HIT@@
print(v)
// @@MISS@@
print("none")
